# Paper Reader — Cursor agent instructions

This is a static frontend + a tiny Node proxy that holds the Anthropic API key
server-side. It runs locally and deploys to Vercel with no code changes.

## Working agreement
- **Before any `git push`, run the full test suite and confirm it passes:**
  `npm test` (152 tests). Do not push if anything fails.
- When the user says a piece of functionality is "good" / "working" (or
  similar), proactively remind them to commit that chunk before moving on.
  Prefer small, focused commits per working feature over one large catch-up
  commit. Only commit when the user confirms.
- Especially when the user brings a prompt for NEW functionality, first ask
  whether to commit the existing/in-progress work before starting the new
  thing, so changes don't pile up into one large mixed commit.

## Run it locally
The app needs an Anthropic API key in the environment. Start with:

```bash
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-... \
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ... \
node dev-server.js
```

Then open http://localhost:3000. No `npm install` is needed — the local server
has zero dependencies. Stop with Ctrl+C.

If the chat returns "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not set", the key wasn't passed on the
command line. Everything except API calls (PDF rendering, URL loading,
highlighting, saved history) works without a key.

## Deploy to Vercel
```bash
npm i -g vercel        # once
vercel                 # first deploy, follow prompts
vercel env add ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   # paste key, select all environments
vercel env add SUPABASE_URL
vercel env add SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
vercel --prod          # redeploy to production with the key live
```

The `api/chat.js` serverless function routes chat to Anthropic via `handler.js`.
The frontend always calls `/api/chat`, so local and prod are identical.

## Architecture (don't break these invariants)
- `index.html`  — entire frontend: PDF.js + Readability.js + reader/chat UI.
  All app logic is one inline <script>. No build step.
- `handler.js`  — shared proxy; routes highlight chat to Sonnet and cheap tasks
  (`task: 'summarize'`, citation match/preview) to Haiku. The `system` field may be a STRING or
  an ARRAY of content blocks; the full-paper block carries
  `cache_control: { type: 'ephemeral' }` for prompt caching. Pass system through
  untouched.
- `store.js`    — Supabase + local persistence (`PaperStore`). Do not bypass for saves.
- `dev-server.js` — local dev server (static files + POST /api/chat, GET /api/config). Zero deps.
- `api/chat.js` — Vercel serverless function; reuses handler.js.
- `api/config.js` — returns public Supabase URL + anon key from env.
- The API key is NEVER in the frontend. Keep it server-side only.

## Storage model
- **Identity:** real Google sign-in via Supabase Auth (`signInWithOAuth`).
 All data is scoped by the authenticated Supabase USER ID. Never hand-roll raw
 Google OAuth; setup/invariants/gotchas live in `docs/AUTH_SETUP.md`.
- **Supabase (primary when configured):** Postgres tables `documents`,
 `discussions`, `messages`, `read_later`, `ratings`; PDFs in Storage bucket
 `pdfs`. The `owner_email` COLUMN carries the Supabase user id (historical
 name; no migration — old email-keyed data was disposable and dropped).
- **Local backup:** per-user namespaced keys `paperReader.docs.v2.<userId>` /
 `paperReader.readLater.v2.<userId>` (signed-out uses `.local`) + IndexedDB
 `paperReader.files.v2` with `<userId>::`-prefixed keys. Legacy v1 keys are
 dropped once at init (guard flag `paperReader.authMigrated.v2`).
- `persistCurrentDoc()` guard — do not remove; prevents history loss on tab-hide.

## Common tasks
- Change the model: edit the default in `handler.js`.
- Adjust full-paper size cap: `MAX_PAPER_CHARS` in `index.html`.
- The web fetch uses public CORS proxies (allorigins.win, corsproxy.io); if a
  site blocks them, the PDF path is the fallback.
